round-trip time for a target at distance d (t = 2d / c)
  d =    0.10 m  ->  t =      0.667 ns
  d =    1.00 m  ->  t =      6.671 ns
  d =   10.00 m  ->  t =     66.713 ns
  d =  100.00 m  ->  t =    667.128 ns

range step for a timer that counts in ticks of dt (step = c * dt / 2)
  dt =   1000 ps  ->  range step =   149.90 mm
  dt =    100 ps  ->  range step =    14.99 mm
  dt =     10 ps  ->  range step =     1.50 mm

converting measured ticks to distance (tick = 100 ps, pretend)
      0 ticks ->   0.0000 m
      1 ticks ->   0.0150 m
     67 ticks ->   1.0043 m
    667 ticks ->   9.9981 m
   6671 ticks ->  99.9958 m
